h member, a woman named Lula, tries to make the children feel bad for attending church with his mother, Zeebo welcomes Scout and Jem with open arms. He is kind but very quiet.\n\nQuestion: Calpurnia son name in to kill a mockingbird?", "references": ["Zeebo", "James Zeebo"]}, {"input": "Passage: By 1912, major motion-picture companies had set up production near or in Los Angeles.[18] In the early 1900s, most motion picture patents were held by Thomas Edison's Motion Picture Patents Company in New Jersey, and filmmakers were often sued to stop their productions. To escape this, filmmakers began moving out west, where Edison's patents could not be enforced.[19] Also, the weather was ideal and there was quick access to various settings. Los Angeles became the capital of the film industry.[20]\n\nQuestion: When did hollywood become the centre of the film industry?", "references": ["1912", "By 1912"]}, {"input": "Passage: The official 2016 estimate of MSA population of Tri-Cities is 283,846. This is over a 12% increase from 2010. (2016 US MSA estimates) 2017 estimates now show Tri-Cities as over 300,000.\n\nQuestion: What is the population of the tri-cities washington?", "references": ["283,846", "over 300,000"]}, {"input": "Passage: Charlene Holt as Maudie\n\nQuestion: Who played maudie in the movie el dorado?", "references": ["Charlene Holt"]}, {"input": "Passage: Mexico competed at the 2018 Winter Olympics in Pyeongchang, South Korea, from 9 to 25 February 2018, with four competitors in three sports.\n\nQuestion: When does mexico play in the winter olympics?", "references": ["9 to 25 February 2018"]}, {"input": "Passage: The earliest known written documentation of the Chinese abacus dates to the 2nd century BC.[21]\n\nQuestion: When was the abacus invented in ancient china?", "references": ["2nd century BC", "written documentation of the Chinese abacus dates to the 2nd century BC"]}, {"input": "Passage: \n\nYear\nImage\nName\nInducted members\nInducted By[11]\n\n\n198